1
00:00:00,040 --> 00:00:03,260
Good morning ah god it's early.
早上好。啊，天哪，真早。

2
00:00:03,260 --> 00:00:08,240
The only sound surrounding me is the light buzz in the air telling me that the world is waking up along with me.
周围只有轻轻的嗡嗡声，仿佛在告诉我，世界也正和我一起醒来。

3
00:00:08,240 --> 00:00:12,540
No noise no disturbance just peacefulness.
没有噪音，没有打扰，只有宁静。

4
00:00:15,199 --> 00:00:18,199
I'll be honest I do not like waking up at 5 am.
说实话，我并不喜欢早上五点起床。

5
00:00:18,199 --> 00:00:22,279
But the warmer it gets and the closer we are to summer the easier I find it to wake up early.
不过天气越暖，离夏天越近，我就越觉得早起容易一些。

6
00:00:22,279 --> 00:00:29,120
It's almost as if with every ray of sunshine dancing throughout the sky my batteries are filling up again and I'm so much more motivated.
仿佛天空中每一道跳动的阳光都在给我充电，让我更有动力。

7
00:00:29,120 --> 00:00:34,160
So here's my 5 a.m.-ish productive and realistic morning routine on a good day.
所以，这是我状态不错时，五点左右开始的高效而真实的晨间日常。

8
00:00:34,160 --> 00:00:37,399
Because we all know not every day looks like this.
毕竟我们都知道，不是每一天都会是这个样子。

9
00:00:37,399 --> 00:00:41,480
We all have good days and bad days and we all have days where we barely get out of bed.
我们都有好日子和糟糕的日子，也有几乎爬不起床的时候。

10
00:00:41,480 --> 00:00:45,860
We rush through the steps within a routine that we do most necessary and out of the door we go.
有时我们匆匆做完日常里觉得最必要的几个步骤，就出门了。

11
00:00:45,860 --> 00:00:47,419
And there is nothing wrong with that.
这也没有什么不对。

12
00:00:47,419 --> 00:00:54,620
But for my own mental and also physical health I find a structured morning routine that I can stick to on most days highly beneficial.
不过，为了自己的身心状态，我发现大多数日子都能坚持的、有结构的晨间安排很有帮助。

13
00:00:54,620 --> 00:00:58,940
The time that I wake up at may vary but the steps that I do usually look the same.
起床时间可能会变，但我做的步骤通常差不多。

14
00:00:58,940 --> 00:01:03,080
The first thing that I do after waking up is I turn on some music and then I leave my phone in my bedroom.
醒来后我先放点音乐，然后把手机留在卧室。

15
00:01:03,080 --> 00:01:06,040
I try to stay off of it for the first 30 minutes of my day.
我尽量在一天开始的前三十分钟不碰手机。

16
00:01:06,040 --> 00:01:11,420
I always feel like my brain is going at 100 miles per hour and my phone is part of my job.
我总觉得脑子转得飞快，而用手机也是我工作的一部分。

17
00:01:11,420 --> 00:01:17,959
So if I go on it first thing in the morning I find that my stress levels are rising so so high so quickly and I try to avoid just that.
所以，如果早上一醒来就看手机，我会发现压力很快就升上来；这正是我想避免的。

18
00:01:17,959 --> 00:01:22,699
So once I'm up I just try to rehydrate myself with some water and then I go into the bathroom.
起来之后，我先喝点水补充水分，再去浴室。

19
00:01:25,279 --> 00:01:33,800
Now for today's morning routine we're talking about a good day and on a good day I certainly do have a bit more time in my hands than most other day since dental school.
今天说的是状态不错那种早晨；这种时候，我的时间肯定比上牙科学校时的大多数日子宽裕些。

20
00:01:33,800 --> 00:01:39,560
To be completely honest whenever I do have the time within my mornings I like to get ready at home after the gym.
坦白说，只要早上有时间，我喜欢健身后回家再收拾自己。

21
00:01:39,560 --> 00:01:41,720
So I'm not doing a lot before my workout.
所以运动前，我不会做太多准备。

22
00:01:41,720 --> 00:01:46,819
I splash my face with water I put on a little bit of moisturizer just so that my skin feels nice and hydrated.
我用水冲一下脸，涂一点保湿霜，让皮肤感觉舒服、水润。

23
00:01:46,819 --> 00:01:51,319
But my actual skincare routine does not take place up until I'm done with my workout.
不过，真正的护肤步骤要等运动结束之后才做。

24
00:01:51,319 --> 00:01:57,610
I also brush my teeth first thing in the morning as I find the step to really wake me up and get me going.
我一早也会先刷牙，觉得这一步真的能让我清醒、进入状态。

25
00:01:57,620 --> 00:02:02,730
Thank you.
谢谢。（来源自动字幕中的短句，待原声复核。）

26
00:02:02,740 --> 00:02:05,960
And then it's time to pick up my gym fit of the day.
然后就该选今天去健身穿的衣服了。

27
00:02:05,960 --> 00:02:09,799
I think a cute outfit for the gym is so essential to boost your motivation.
我觉得一套好看的健身穿搭，对提升动力很有帮助。

28
00:02:09,799 --> 00:02:15,750
Which is super necessary when you're barely awake and you would much rather be in bed at this time.
尤其当你还没完全醒、这会儿更想待在床上时，就更需要一点动力。

29
00:02:32,659 --> 00:02:35,719
Once that I'm dressed and my hair is done I go and make my bed.
穿好衣服、弄好头发后，我就去整理床铺。

30
00:02:35,719 --> 00:02:39,920
This is a habit that I really try to establish within my morning routine for the past few months.
过去几个月，我一直想把这个习惯融入晨间日常。

31
00:02:39,920 --> 00:02:46,159
And thanks to sticking with it and incorporating it with habit stacking it'll really earned its solid spot within my routine.
坚持做，再把它接在已有习惯后面，终于让它在我的日常里有了固定位置。

32
00:02:46,159 --> 00:02:52,400
Making my bed makes me feel more structured and I feel like as if I would be starting the day with the right mindset through and through.
整理床铺让我更有条理，也感觉自己以合适的心态开始了这一天。

33
00:02:52,400 --> 00:02:58,579
Also at night when the sun goes sleep I feel so much better going into my bedroom and not finding it to be an absolute mess.
到了晚上，太阳落下，我走进卧室时看到的不是一团糟，感觉也会好很多。

34
00:02:58,579 --> 00:03:01,160
So this is a win win situation.
所以，这是一件两头都受益的事。
